  "description": "HUQCON crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H114 Co2 Dy5 N10 O40,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1D (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2D (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1D (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3D (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 1.593-3.837 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 35.50-122.19°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C78H114Co2Dy5N10O40·4(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
